  "contributors": "Christopher Daniel Pang supplied the PAL v2.4 frame and direction questions, RPL old/detail split, BLA boundary accounting and the active construction key. Hearthline derived the adaptive maximum principle, square spike obstruction, return price and signed physical portion.",
  "formal_scope": "Two independently fixed implications to stock Mathlib RH. The first assumes one selectable earlier interval meeting the integer square-root price at each head. The second assumes one nonpositive interval per sufficiently late head.",
  "paper_scope": "Certain balanced positive and negative square marks force an oriented price of order width times mark size through widths below (2*pi^2/9-eps) times the smooth root. On slowly shrinking windows the selected negative contribution has exactly the critical recovery factor. The remaining total signed price at all heads is open.",
